[center]
[size=6][color=#74C7F5][b]BODY CHANGE NG · v1.2.0[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][color=#B7DDF2]Change the player's and NPCs' BodySlide presets and body skins, edit the player's tint masks in real time, and distribute BodySlide presets and body skins to NPCs using editable conditions[/color][/size]

[color=#9AD7F5][b]NATIVE IN-GAME GUI  •  GAMEPAD SUPPORT  •  RULE-BASED NPC DISTRIBUTION[/b][/color]
[color=#B7DDF2][b]CBBE 3BA  •  BHUNP / UNP  •  UBE 2.0  •  HIMBO  •  SAM  •  VANILLA FEMALE / MALE[/b][/color]
[/center]

[line]

[size=5][color=#5FB8E8][b]OVERVIEW[/b][/color][/size]

Body Change NG is a native SKSE plugin for changing BodySlide morph presets, actor skin textures, optional genital-addon skins, and the player's RaceMenu tint layers from one in-game interface. It also includes an ordered rule editor for distributing body presets and skins to NPCs.

Body shape remains RaceMenu BodyMorph data. Version 1.2.0 replaces the old general-purpose skin repaint pipeline with an actor-native TextureSet → ArmorAddon → Skin Armor graph. The selected skin becomes the NPC base's normal skin source, so naked body, hands, feet, and face rebuild through Skyrim's own system without BCNG tracking which gloves, boots, or outfits are equipped.

[line]

[size=5][color=#5FB8E8][b]WHAT'S NEW IN 1.2.0[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Native Skin Armor/TXST backend[/b] — BCNG deep-clones the actor's current provider graph, preserves every original texture channel, overlays only the DDS parts supplied by the selected pack, and attaches the private graph at the NPC ActorBase.
[*][b]Equipment-independent base skin[/b] — changing clothes is no longer a trigger for repainting the normal body skin. When an outfit reveals the real body, Skyrim rebuilds it from the already selected Skin Armor.
[*][b]Exact body-part routing[/b] — body, hands, feet, face, 3BA vagina/anus, BHUNP vagina/anus/canal, beast tails, and external genital addons have separate roles. A missing or ambiguous role is never redirected to another part.
[*][b]Conventional-body versus UBE catalog[/b] — Legacy means a pack using Skyrim's conventional [font=Courier New]actors\character[/font] texture tree, including CBBE/3BA, BHUNP/UNP, vanilla female/male, HIMBO, and SAM. Only an explicit [font=Courier New]!UBE\Body[/font] or [font=Courier New]!UBE\Head[/font] tree is UBE. Exact material routing is derived from the actor at apply time, not from the pack name.
[*][b]Safe partial packs[/b] — every part and material channel is optional. Missing DDS files keep the current provider value instead of borrowing a body, hand, foot, face, or genital texture.
[*][b]UBE 2.0 graph support[/b] — the verified slot-53 body plus separate hand/foot ArmorAddons use the UBE Body atlas, while the Head atlas targets the face. Private TXST synthesis is limited to verified canonical UBE naked models.
[*][b]RSV-aware ownership[/b] — Racial Skin Variance may remain the provider. BCNG rebuilds from current RSV forms when they change and restores only pointers it still owns; its bounded face bridge does not create or delete RSV's saved keys.
[*][b]Independent appearance features[/b] — body morph, native base skin, player tint, male SOS/TNG, female futanari, RSV face, and outfit correction use separate state and work channels. Clearing one does not reset the others.
[*][b]Reliable NPC distribution[/b] — BodyMorph stays reference-scoped, while native skin is ActorBase-scoped. A result is recorded only after its operation succeeds, and an unchanged Body or Skin category preserves its saved result.
[*][b]Safer rule editing and saving[/b] — starter rules can be edited, reordered, and deleted; new IDs do not collide; earlier broad rules show a shadowing warning; built-in names follow Korean, English, or Simplified Chinese; JSON saves use validated temporary files and atomic replacement.
[*][b]Explicit compatibility boundaries[/b] — verified Skyrim SE 1.5.97 and AE 1.6.x layouts through 1.6.1179 are supported. RaceMenu interface generations are dispatched separately and unknown layouts fail closed. Skyrim VR is not built or supported.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][color=#5FB8E8][b]FEATURES[/b][/color][/size]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]Body Presets[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*]Select the player or a loaded NPC and preview compatible BodySlide presets.
[*]Low/high values interpolate by actor weight.
[*]Preview, commit, and outfit correction use separate owned BodyMorph keys.
[*]Repeated application reaches the same absolute result without clearing morph keys owned by other mods.
[*]Body preset XML classification and runtime BodyFamily checks remain independent from skin-pack classification.
[/list]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]Body Skins[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*]Apply separate skin packs to the player or loaded NPCs.
[*]Native body, hand, foot, far-skin, and optional face TextureSets are cloned from the current provider; unrelated channels stay intact.
[*]Conventional CBBE/3BA, BHUNP/UNP, vanilla, HIMBO, and SAM texture trees are grouped as Legacy. UBE is detected only from the explicit [font=Courier New]!UBE[/font] atlas namespace.
[*]CBBE 3BA and BHUNP/UNP genital/anal atlases route only to their exact matching geometry.
[*]HIMBO or SAM skin and SOS/TNG slot-52 textures may live in one pack. Vanilla male skin is also supported; the live addon path chooses Regular, Muscular, Smurf, race, and elder variants.
[*]Argonian and Khajiit packs are filtered by race and sex, and the body atlas also reaches the matching native tail role.
[*]Default Skin restores the captured provider graph without touching BodyMorph, tint, futanari, or foreign override ownership.
[/list]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]Futanari Skin[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*]The tab appears only for a detected supported female addon: UBE SOS/TNG, UBE/CBBE TRX, or CBBE 3BA ERF.
[*]The genital skin choice is separate from the full BodySkin choice.
[*]Removing the addon keeps the selection; re-equipping its supported type reapplies the saved skin.
[*]Missing channels remain controlled by the addon's original material.
[/list]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]Player Tint Masks[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*]Install multiple RaceMenu tint-mask packs and choose per tint layer.
[*]Edit color and opacity immediately and restore the exact captured original value.
[*]Confirmed layers return after RaceMenu rebuilds the player.
[*]Tint editing is player-only. Overlay-based makeup is not supported by this tab.
[/list]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]NPC Distribution[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*]Rules are evaluated top to bottom; the first match owns both category decisions.
[*]Body and Skin can each distribute a pool, explicitly use Default, be excluded, or remain unchanged.
[*]Conditions include sex, custom followers, elders, plugin, race, faction, keyword, class, name, and exact NPC base FormID.
[*]One entry is fixed; multiple entries produce a stable per-NPC result.
[*]Apply rules to loaded NPCs now, or save a next-launch draft without silently replacing the current session's active rules.
[*]Sample and user rules have the same edit, reorder, and delete behavior.
[/list]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]UI and Input[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*]Korean, English, and Simplified Chinese interface text.
[*]Configurable F7 shortcut with Ctrl, Shift, and Ctrl+Shift combinations.
[*]Mouse, keyboard/WASD, and gamepad D-pad navigation with confirm/cancel.
[*]Native IME input, Unicode names and search, favorites, and favorites-only filters.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][color=#5FB8E8][b]REQUIREMENTS[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*]Skyrim SE 1.5.97 or a supported Skyrim AE 1.6.x runtime through 1.6.1179
[*]Matching SKSE64
[*]Address Library for SKSE Plugins matching the game runtime
[*]RaceMenu matching the game runtime, with BodyMorph and NiOverride/Override
[*]BodySlide presets and compatible TRI files built with [b]Build Morphs[/b]
[/list]

[b]Skyrim VR is not supported.[/b]

[line]

[size=5][color=#5FB8E8][b]INSTALLATION AND UPDATE[/b][/color][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install the Release ZIP with MO2 and keep its folder structure intact.
[*]When updating, preserve personal asset folders and [font=Courier New]SKSE\Plugins\BodyChangeNGdistribution.json[/font] if they are stored inside the main mod.
[*]Enable the mod, launch through SKSE, and press F7.
[/list]

Version 1.2.0 is a separate architectural line from 1.1.4. Do not combine DLLs from the two versions. Existing settings, distribution rules, favorites, and co-save identifiers are migrated in place. Keep the old DLL backup as the safest rollback point for a save not yet continued extensively under 1.2.0.

[line]

[size=5][color=#5FB8E8][b]ADDING ASSETS[/b][/color][/size]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]BodySlide Presets[/b][/color][/size]
[font=Courier New]CalienteTools\BodySlide\SliderPresets\*.xml[/font]

Use standard BodySlide preset XML and build the matching body/outfit TRI data with Build Morphs.

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]CBBE 3BA and BHUNP/UNP Female BodySkin Packs[/b][/color][/size]

[font=Courier New]BodySkin\My Skin\Textures\actors\character\female\femalebody_1.dds[/font]
[font=Courier New]BodySkin\My Skin\Textures\actors\character\female\femalehands_1.dds[/font]
[font=Courier New]BodySkin\My Skin\Textures\actors\character\female\femalehead.dds[/font]

Copy the source mod's original texture tree. The top-level folder is the display name and stable-ID source.

For CBBE 3BA, [font=Courier New]femalebody_etc_v2_1[/font] plus [font=Courier New]_msn[/font], [font=Courier New]_sk[/font], and [font=Courier New]_s[/font] is the vagina/anus atlas. For BHUNP/UNP, preserve [font=Courier New]BakaUNP\VaginalAnalCanal2[/font] with the same suffixes for vagina/anus/canal. These do not classify the pack and never replace the regular body, hands, feet, or face.

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]UBE 2.0 BodySkin Packs[/b][/color][/size]

[font=Courier New]BodySkin\My UBE Skin\Textures\!UBE\Body\femalebody_1_d, _n, or _sk.dds[/font]
[font=Courier New]BodySkin\My UBE Skin\Textures\!UBE\Head\femalehead_d, _n, or _sk.dds[/font]

Keep Legacy and UBE assets in separate top-level pack folders.

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]HIMBO and SAM BodySkin plus SOS/TNG[/b][/color][/size]

Keep the HIMBO or SAM body/hand/foot/face tree and SOS/TNG addon folders under the same skin pack. Vanilla male skins use the same conventional texture layout. BCNG never joins textures across packs.

[font=Courier New]BodySkin\My Male Skin\Textures\actors\character\SOS\&lt;addon name&gt;\malegenitals_1*[/font]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]Futanari Packs[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*]UBE SOS/TNG: [font=Courier New]Futanari\&lt;pack&gt;\Textures\!UBE\Body\malebody_1_d, _n, or _sk.dds[/font]
[*]TRX: [font=Courier New]Futanari\&lt;pack&gt;\Textures\&#91;TRX&#93; Futa addon\Regular\Default\schlong*[/font]
[*]ERF: [font=Courier New]Futanari\&lt;pack&gt;\Textures\ERF_Futanari\FairSkinCBBE\futanari_schlong*[/font]
[/list]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]Tint Packs[/b][/color][/size]

[font=Courier New]TintMask\&lt;pack&gt;\textures\actors\character\character assets\tintmasks\*.dds[/font]

Files added while Skyrim is running appear after pressing [b]Refresh[/b] on the matching tab.

[line]

[size=5][color=#5FB8E8][b]COMPATIBILITY NOTES[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Racial Skin Variance[/b] — BCNG treats the current RSV graph as a provider and maintains a bounded face bridge. UBE 2.0's own requirement to exclude its player race from RSV ([font=Courier New]PLAYER VANILLA[/font]) still applies.
[*][b]SOS/TNG/TRX/ERF[/b] — external genital geometry remains reference-scoped and equipment-aware, separate from ActorBase-scoped body skin.
[*][b]Mu Dynamic NormalMap[/b] — supported companion normal bundles remain with the selected cached normal.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][color=#5FB8E8][b]SAVE AND OWNERSHIP SCOPE[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*]BodyMorph and external genital addons are actor-reference scoped.
[*]Native BodySkin is NPC ActorBase scoped. References sharing one base share one native skin selection.
[*]Direct choices and evaluated NPC results belong to the current SKSE co-save.
[*]Distribution rules are stored in [font=Courier New]Data\SKSE\Plugins\BodyChangeNGdistribution.json[/font].
[*]Settings and rule JSON remain supported; they are unrelated to the removed skin-pack manifest.
[/list]

